---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Heading from "../components/Heading.astro";
import Prose from "../components/Prose.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

import muralPhoto from "../assets/james-button-mural.jpg";
import CameraIcon from "../assets/svg/camera.svg";
---

<Layout pageTitle="About">
  <Section className="wrapper flow" as="div">
    <Heading level={1} emphasis>About James</Heading>

    <Prose>
      <figure slot="figure">
        <Image
          src={muralPhoto}
          width={480}
          alt="James Button holding an oboe in front of the Tontasin Renance mural in San Francisco, CA"
          class="prose--image"
          format="avif"
          densities={[1, 1.5, 2]}
        />
        <figcaption><CameraIcon /> David Kim</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>
        James Button was appointed Associate Principal Oboe of the San Francisco
        Symphony in September 2017. A native of Australia, he made his solo
        debut with the Melbourne Symphony Orchestra at the age of seventeen.
      </p>

      <p>
        Mr. Button studied at Temple University and the Juilliard School, where
        his principal teachers included Jonathan Blumenfeld and Eugene Izotov.
        He has also studied with John Mack, John de Lancie, and Joseph Turner.
      </p>

      <p>
        Prior to joining the San Francisco Symphony, Mr. Button was a member of
        the Nashville Symphony, the Santa Fe Opera Orchestra, and the New World
        Symphony. He has appeared as Guest Principal Oboe with the Chicago
        Symphony Orchestra, Philadelphia Orchestra, and Los Angeles
        Philharmonic.
      </p>

      <p>
        An active performer both nationally and internationally, Mr. Button has
        appeared at the Verbier, Edinburgh, and Tanglewood Music Festivals, as
        well as Italy’s Spoleto Festival dei Due Mondi and the Santa Fe Chamber
        Music Festival. His live recording of Jennifer Higdon’s Oboe Concerto
        with the Nashville Symphony received a Grammy Award in 2018.
      </p>

      <p>
        In addition to his orchestral career, Mr. Button has enjoyed a diverse
        freelance career, including recording projects with Björk and Willie
        Nelson, performances on Broadway in Fiddler on the Roof, and guest
        principal appearances with his hometown orchestra, the Melbourne
        Symphony Orchestra.
      </p>

      <p>Mr. Button is a Marigaux artist and performs on a 920A model oboe.</p>
    </Prose>
  </Section>
</Layout>
